@startuml
title ioScope System - Component Diagram

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam shadowing false

component "ioScope Application" as ScopeApp {
  component "ioQtScopeWindow\n<<UI host>>" as QtWindow
  component "ioScopeShell\n<<CLI shell>>" as Shell
  component "ioOscilloscopeController" as Controller
  component "ioOscilloscopeModel" as Model
  component "ioCompactOscilloscopeView" as CompactView
  component "ioDetailedOscilloscopeView" as DetailedView
  component "ioFilterPipeline" as FilterPipeline
  component "ioWaveformGenerator" as Generator
  component "ioGeneratedWaveformSource" as GeneratedSource
  component "ioFileWaveformSource" as FileSource
  component "ioFtdiWaveformSource" as FtdiSource
  component "ioLiveOscilloscopeSession" as LiveSession
  component "ioPipelineController\n<<live acquisition pipeline>>" as PipelineController

  () "oscilloscopeControl" as OscilloscopeControl
  () "ioOscilloscopeView" as ViewContract
  () "signalProcessing" as SignalProcessing
  () "ioSignalSource" as SignalSource
  () "liveAcquisitionControl" as LiveAcquisitionControl
}

OscilloscopeControl - Controller
ViewContract - CompactView
ViewContract - DetailedView
SignalProcessing - FilterPipeline
SignalSource - GeneratedSource
SignalSource - FileSource
SignalSource - FtdiSource
LiveAcquisitionControl - LiveSession

QtWindow ..> OscilloscopeControl : UI events
Shell ..> OscilloscopeControl : shell commands
QtWindow ..> ViewContract : host active view
Controller ..> ViewContract : render(state)
Controller --> Model : update + query state
Controller ..> LiveAcquisitionControl : start() / stop() / refresh()
Model ..> SignalProcessing : apply scale + offset
Model --> Generator : refreshSamples()
Generator ..> SignalSource : select source
LiveSession --> PipelineController : configure / start / stop

note bottom of ScopeApp
This is the whole-system component view for ioScope.
The UI, controller, model, filter pipeline, source adapters,
and live acquisition session are shown together as one application.
end note

note bottom of PipelineController
The detailed producer-consumer internals of the live
pipeline are documented separately in the dedicated
multithreaded pipeline component diagrams.
end note
@enduml
